# AgriVoice — Showcase Build Overview

AgriVoice turns scattered, outdated market gossip into a **real-time, comparable,
confidence-scored crop-price picture** for Ethiopian farmers. The long-term moat
is the **crowd-data loop** — a growing base of real reported sale prices — not the
AI. This build showcases that loop live.

## What we are demoing (the pivot — read this)

The original concept was voice-first (farmer speaks → STT → LLM → TTS). **For this
showcase, voice is PARKED.** Amharic STT is the single most likely thing to fail
on stage, and it isn't what proves the idea. Instead we demo the data engine:

> **The money shot:** a human **agent** enters a farmer's price in the data-entry
> **portal**, and the public **showcase dashboard** updates in front of the judges —
> new price, new confidence %, new trend, live on the map.

That one loop proves the crowd-data moat. Everything we build serves it.

## Locked decisions (do not re-litigate)

1. **"Live" = polling.** The dashboard and live list re-fetch every ~2–3s. No
   websockets/Reverb — it must survive conference wifi. See owner files.
2. **Named agents, light login.** Each data-entry agent has a name + PIN so every
   entry is attributed ("entered by Nati"). This powers the attribution and
   flag-outlier / anti-poisoning story. No full user auth beyond this.
3. **One host laptop.** The showcase laptop runs Laravel + SQLite and serves the
   dashboard on the projector; agents enter data from their own laptops by
   hitting the host's LAN IP (`http://<host-ip>:8000`). See `050-infra-devops.mdc`.

## In scope (the spine)

1. **Data-entry portal** — agent picks crop + market, enters price / date / source,
   submits. Owner: **Gezachew**.
2. **Live data list** — master table of every entry, newest first, with agent
   attribution, crop/market filters, and a flag-outlier action. Owner: **Nati**.
3. **Showcase dashboard** — price cards (price + confidence % + report count +
   last-updated), market map, trend arrows, auto-refreshing. Owner: **Tsegaye**.
4. **Market intelligence backend** — aggregation, confidence scoring, nearby-market
   comparison, moving-average trend, agent auth, seed data. Owner: **Nba**.

## Out of scope (say it out loud — nobody builds these)

- Voice pipeline (STT / TTS / LLM). Parked — see `030-ai-llm-safety.mdc` for when
  it returns. A single canned voice clip is an *optional* stretch, never on the
  critical path.
- Cooperative dashboard, trader/exporter API, NGO reporting, agri-input cross-sell
  — that's the *business model*, not the demo.
- Real user auth / accounts, payments, admin panels, settings pages.
- Any crop or market outside the list below.

## Fixed scope

- **Crops:** Teff, Coffee (only).
- **Markets:** Adama, Addis Ababa, Jimma (only) — 2 crops × 3 markets = 6 dashboard tiles.
- **Currency/unit:** ETB per quintal, everywhere.

